\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

We showed that knowledge conflict signals in multilingual LLMs are linearly detectable across languages and that the transfer asymmetry (ZH$\to$EN $>$ EN$\to$ZH by ${\sim}$7~pp) is consistent with the XNLI baseline, reflecting general cross-lingual structure.
In Llama, causal influence is localized to L13 (41\% depth) while detection peaks at L28; steering failed in Qwen and Gemma despite 88.9\% probe accuracy, demonstrating that detectability does not imply causal relevance.
